    "result_text": "The change is implemented and its test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a derived, read-only field: a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`. This follows the exact pattern already used for other derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`).\n\nThree edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the JSON response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getCheckDigit()` that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode` (returns `null` when no code is assigned).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` wiring `checkDigit` from `owner.getCheckDigit()`.\n\n## Test results\n\n- The new spec test **`Cp31Tests`** (recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit) **passes**.\n- Full suite: **44 of 45 pass**. The one failure, **`Cp28Tests.coreRejectsIdentityCollision`**, is **pre-existing and unrelated** \u2014 it exercises a different, not-yet-implemented spec (\"consolidate duplicate detection into a single `identityKey`\"). It fails because the current baseline includes `householdId` in `identityKey`, so two owners with the same phone but different name/address aren't treated as duplicates. My change touches only the `checkDigit` serialization path and cannot affect duplicate-detection behavior.\n\nThe assigned change fully satisfies the specification and its tests are green.",
